<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20993] Stranded Replay Request Causing Server Recreate Stale MDT Object after MDS Reboot</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20993</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The Mechanism is the following:&lt;br/&gt;
1. A client opens a file with O_CREAT. After the reply, the client keeps that open request on its &lt;b&gt;replay list&lt;/b&gt; so it can be replayed if the MDT restarts. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. The file is unlinked and closed, so the server destroys the MDT object and its OST objects. Normally mdc_close() also clears the request's rq_replay, which drops it from the list. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Client bug:&lt;/b&gt; if the client has no md_open_data (mod) for that open, the close goes through but rq_replay is never cleared. That happens, for example, when obd_mod_alloc() fails in mdc_set_open_replay_data(): cannot allocate md_open_data, then couldn't find open req; expecting close error. The dead open stays on the replay list. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;4. At the next MDT restart the client replays it (MSG_REPLAY). It is a committed open, so it is handled inline, and the replayed N reqs counter does not count it. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Server bug:&lt;/b&gt; in mdt_reint_open(), the replay branch calls mdt_open_by_fid(), gets -ENOENT, and then does No object(1), continue as regular open. That re-creates the destroyed FID. Because it is a replay, no_create=1: no OST objects are allocated, and the client's saved layout is written verbatim. The result is the stale entry. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. Second client bug:&lt;/b&gt; a failed or refused open replay is &lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; dropped. It is retried at every MDT restart, so each patching reboot can resurrect the same files again. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reproducer: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;client &lt;br/&gt;
lctl set_param fail_loc=2147485708                  # 0x8000080c, fires once &lt;br/&gt;
python3 -c 'import os,time; p="/fs144/x.tmp"; fd=os.open(p,os.O_RDWR|os.O_CREAT,0o644); os.write(fd,b"x"); time.sleep(5); os.unlink(p); os.close(fd)' &lt;br/&gt;
lctl set_param fail_loc=0; sync &lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;MDS: plain (failover) restart &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Also attaching my tentative fix patches here&lt;/p&gt;</description>
